duces the real committed removal entry under the old voter configuration.','b-election':'Actual campaigns establish initial and remaining-node leadership; no role assignment.'},obligation_relation_kind='consumption',counterevidence=['StepDownOnRemoval=true demotes the removed leader.','Proposal path checks local membership, but read singleton branch only checks voter cardinality.','An application may stop routing reads to removed nodes; no such routing layer is supplied by RawNode.','Read requests may be lost, so no-output control is permitted, not a liveness violation.'],unknowns=['Formal fresh execution and correspondence are required; exploration is not property evidence.','No application client return or stale state-machine value is measured.'],priority=3,trigger_rationale='Exploration 4d73d083187f41999c27b05b1222ce12 completed the actual removal/write history and observed a removed StateLeader emitting index 3 after the remaining voter applied index 5; this motivates a narrower authority-support obligation, not a global linearizability conclusion.',disposition='ready_for_check',preferred_check='controlled_schedule')\nclaim=dict(id='claim-removed-safe-read',kind='obligation',concern='implementation_semantics',description='A ReadOnlySafe request must not release a ReadState solely on the serving node local state when that node is not an eligible voter in the active singleton configuration and it has obtained no fresh support from the sole eligible voter for that request.',source_ids=['s-read-mode','s-read-contract','s-read-entry','s-confchange-api','s-removal-option','s-leader-entry','s-tracker'],scope=dict(description='Public RawNode safe-read output after locally applied committed removal leaves another node as sole voter. Continued invocation of the library API is in scope; no integration routing layer is assumed.',assumptions=['Serialized calls and application of committed configuration through ApplyConfChange.','Distinct nonempty read context; static singleton configuration after removal; no lease-based reads.','StepDownOnRemoval=false is the target configuration; true is a permitted no-output control.','Caller continues using the removed RawNode rather than imposing an external shutdown policy.'],excluded=['Client-return linearizability, physical persistence or arbitrary crashes.','Progress guarantee for the true-option control.','A claim that every deployment continues serving removed nodes.']),pending=[],grounding=dict(source_ids=['s-leader-entry','s-tracker','s-recovery-config','s-read-result'],expectation_ids=['s-read-mode','s-read-contract','s-read-entry','s-confchange-api','s-removal-option'],binding_ids=['binding-singleton-authority'],derivation='ReadOnlySafe guarantees reads through quorum communication; Node/RawNode describe the returned request-specific index as a safe application barrier. A sole voter can supply local quorum authority only if it is the serving node. Config changes take effect when applied, and StepDownOnRemoval makes role demotion optional without declaring that unsafe read results are permitted. Therefore a removed node with no fresh sole-voter support cannot use only local state as safe authority. This requirement allows silence/forwarding/rejection and does not infer liveness or demand a stale client result.',applicability='At the RawNode library boundary, ReadIndex has no stated membership precondition or automatic Stop, and ApplyConfChange documentation requires applying the removal rather than forbidding later API calls. External routing that stops removed nodes is a deployment mitigation outside this scope. The check uses actual committed removal, callbacks, elections and ordered storage; it does not arbitrarily install a config.',unresolved=['No external service contract is inspected; deployment consequences remain excluded.'],conflicts=[],alternatives=['Enabling StepDownOnRemoval is an existing protection and will be measured as a no-output control.']))\nbinding=dict(id='binding-si